Unsupported aggregate macro parameters fail explicitly with their expansion
path, preserving the preceding output; they are not accepted with fake meaning.
-- input.roff --
.de M
prefix
\\$@
..
.M arg
-- error.txt --
unsupported macro parameter
-- expected.txt --
groff.TokenText "prefix"
error evaluate token 1 (macro M / body line 2): unsupported macro parameter "@"
-- parsed.txt --
*groff.TokenMacroDefinition ".de M\nprefix\n\\\\$@\n.."
*groff.TokenUnknownControl ".M arg"
